{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-98164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the principal $9$th root of unity." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f75c4c5c156d3c2358e1923507d25f5553beef6f8209a84d0e392a9f8598291"} {"question" "q-98164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $z$ be a $9$th root of unity. This means that \n\n$$\n{z}^{9}=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the complex number $1$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta }.$ Notice that $|1|=1$ and $\\operatorname{arg}⁡(1)=0.$ Hence, \n\n$$\n1={e}^{\\text{i}(0+2k\\pi )}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is an integer. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{9}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}}\\,⟹\\,z=({e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}})^{1/9}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}/9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe principal root corresponds to $k=1,$ and is therefore equal to ${e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/9}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f75c4c5c156d3c2358e1923507d25f5553beef6f8209a84d0e392a9f8598291"} {"question" "q-98164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57dd46a5e6d8e99dbe0ad13a4025b3d790f12a0859dfc70e2b91b1069e04cd94"} {"question" "q-98164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f75c4c5c156d3c2358e1923507d25f5553beef6f8209a84d0e392a9f8598291"} {"question" "q-98164" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}"] ["math" "{e}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/9}"] ["ma