},\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is an integer. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{12}={e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}}\\,⟹\\,z=({e}^{2k\\pi \\text{i}})^{1/12}={e}^{k\\pi \\text{i}/6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe principal root corresponds to $k=1,$ and is therefore equal to ${e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f75c4c5c156d3c2358e1923507d25f5553beef6f8209a84d0e392a9f8598291"} {"question" "q-97998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "57dd46a5e6d8e99dbe0ad13a4025b3d790f12a0859dfc70e2b91b1069e04cd94"} {"question" "q-97998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f75c4c5c156d3c2358e1923507d25f5553beef6f8209a84d0e392a9f8598291"} {"question" "q-97998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/12}"] ["math" "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/24}"] ["math" "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}"] ["math" "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}"] ["math" "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/8}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f75c4c5c156d3c2358e1923507d25f5553beef6f8209a84d0e392a9f8598291"} {"question" "q-97998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980994/state.json" "file_sha256" "7f75c4c5c156d3c2358e1923507d25f5553beef6f8209a84d0e392a9f8598291"} {"question" "q-107494" "field" nil "a